# C# async/await rules (global + PDFVite-specific)

## 🎯 Primary directive

Prioritize non-blocking, high-throughput async I/O. Eliminate sync-over-async, maximize parallelism, and control concurrency.

## 🚫 Critical anti-patterns (never generate)

### 1) Blocking async code (thread pool starvation)

```csharp
// Do not block on async
.Result
.Wait()
.GetAwaiter().GetResult()
Task.Run(() => await SomeAsyncMethod()) // unnecessary for I/O
```

### 2) Async void (silent failures)

```csharp
// Only valid for UI/events
public async void ProcessMessage(Message msg) // use Task instead
```

### 3) Sequential async when parallel is possible

```csharp
// Inefficient
var user = await GetUserAsync(id);
var permissions = await GetPermissionsAsync(id);

// Preferred
var userTask = GetUserAsync(id);
var permissionsTask = GetPermissionsAsync(id);
await Task.WhenAll(userTask, permissionsTask).ConfigureAwait(false);
```

## ✅ Required patterns

### Async all the way

- Return `Task<T>`/`Task`; avoid `async void`
- Add `CancellationToken cancellationToken = default` to public async APIs
- Use `ConfigureAwait(false)` in library/service layers

### Parallel operations

```csharp
var userTask = _userService.GetUserAsync(userId, cancellationToken);
var permissionsTask = _authService.GetPermissionsAsync(userId, cancellationToken);
await Task.WhenAll(userTask, permissionsTask).ConfigureAwait(false);
```

### Controlled concurrency (bulk work)

```csharp
const int maxConcurrency = 10;
using var semaphore = new SemaphoreSlim(maxConcurrency);
var tasks = ids.Select(async id =>
{
    await semaphore.WaitAsync(cancellationToken).ConfigureAwait(false);
    try { return await _svc.ProcessAsync(id, cancellationToken).ConfigureAwait(false); }
    finally { semaphore.Release(); }
});
var results = await Task.WhenAll(tasks).ConfigureAwait(false);
```

### Proper exception handling

```csharp
public async Task ProcessAsync(Data data, CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)
{
    try
    {
        await _repository.SaveAsync(data, cancellationToken).ConfigureAwait(false);
        await _notificationService.NotifyAsync(data.UserId, cancellationToken).ConfigureAwait(false);
    }
    catch (OperationCanceledException)
    {
        _logger.LogInformation("Operation cancelled for data {DataId}", data.Id);
        throw; // rethrow cancellation
    }
    catch (Exception ex)
    {
        _logger.LogError(ex, "Failed to process data {DataId}", data.Id);
        throw; // rethrow after logging
    }
}
```

### ValueTask for hot paths

```csharp
public ValueTask<CachedData> GetCachedAsync(string key)
{
    if (_cache.TryGetValue(key, out var data)) return new ValueTask<CachedData>(data);
    return new ValueTask<CachedData>(LoadFromDatabaseAsync(key));
}
```

## 🔧 Implementation guidance

### Database (EF Core)

- Use async variants: `FirstOrDefaultAsync`, `ToListAsync`, `SaveChangesAsync`
- Include `CancellationToken`
- Use `ConfigureAwait(false)` in service/library code

### HTTP

- Use async `HttpClient` APIs and timeouts/retries
- Handle `OperationCanceledException`

### Controllers/Endpoints

- Make actions async, accept `CancellationToken`
- Use appropriate HTTP status codes

### Services

- Implement async interfaces; log with structured context
- Consider `ValueTask<T>` on hot paths

### Testing

- Async test methods; test cancellation and exception paths

## 🧭 Enforcement snippets

### Method signatures

```csharp
public async Task<ActionResult<UserData>> GetUserDataAsync(
    int userId,
    CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)
{
    // ...
}
```

### EF operations

```csharp
var user = await _dbContext.Users
    .FirstOrDefaultAsync(u => u.Id == userId, cancellationToken)
    .ConfigureAwait(false);
await _dbContext.SaveChangesAsync(cancellationToken).ConfigureAwait(false);
```

### Bulk with concurrency control

```csharp
const int maxConcurrency = 10;
using var gate = new SemaphoreSlim(maxConcurrency, maxConcurrency);
var tasks = items.Select(async x =>
{
    await gate.WaitAsync(cancellationToken).ConfigureAwait(false);
    try { return await ProcessAsync(x, cancellationToken).ConfigureAwait(false); }
    finally { gate.Release(); }
});
return (await Task.WhenAll(tasks).ConfigureAwait(false)).ToList();
```

## 🏷️ PDFVite-specific rules

### Handlers

- Include `CancellationToken` parameter
- Use EF async with `ConfigureAwait(false)`
- Return `Results<...>`; never block

Example

```csharp
public static async Task<Results<Ok<T>, BadRequest<ApiResponse>>> Handle(
    IAuthContext auth,
    ILogger<MyHandler> logger,
    MainApiDbContext db,
    CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)
{
    if (!auth.IsAuthenticated) throw new UnauthorizedAccessException();
    var user = await db.User.FindAsync(new object[] { auth.UserId }, cancellationToken)
        .ConfigureAwait(false);
    if (user is null) return TypedResults.BadRequest(new ApiResponse { Message = "Invalid session", Key = "invalid-session" });
    return TypedResults.Ok(/* map */);
}
```

### Services

- Async methods only; add cancellation
- Log with structured context and rethrow
- Prefer parallel queries where independent

### Bulk operations (repo standard)

```csharp
const int MaxConcurrency = 10;
using var gate = new SemaphoreSlim(MaxConcurrency, MaxConcurrency);
var tasks = users.Select(async u =>
{
    await gate.WaitAsync(ct).ConfigureAwait(false);
    try { return await ProcessSingleUserAsync(u, ct).ConfigureAwait(false); }
    finally { gate.Release(); }
});
return (await Task.WhenAll(tasks).ConfigureAwait(false)).ToList();
```

### Anti-patterns to watch

- Sync-over-async in handlers or middlewares
- Missing `ConfigureAwait(false)` in library/service code
- Missing `CancellationToken` parameters
- Sequential EF queries that can run in parallel

## ✅ Lint checklist (Cursor must verify)

- [ ] No `.Result`/`.Wait()`/`.GetAwaiter().GetResult()`
- [ ] No `async void` (except events)
- [ ] `Task.WhenAll()` used where possible
- [ ] `ConfigureAwait(false)` used in service/library code
- [ ] `CancellationToken` present on public async APIs
- [ ] Concurrency limits for bulk operations
- [ ] Exceptions logged with structured context and rethrown

## 📊 Expected results

- Response time: 10–100x faster
- Throughput: 50–100x increase
